  "limitations": [
    "Only two fixed tasks per provider; no confidence intervals, provider ranking, causal attribution or general savings claim.",
    "Full corpus is eight selected public project documents, not a comprehensive repository or autonomous research workload.",
    "Prompts use identical questions/instructions and verbatim common source IDs; different document context lengths are the intended treatment.",
    "QMD lexical selection was fixed before answers; task B focused omits the separate retrieval-evaluation document, and rubric deductions remain recorded.",
    "Native default context, system policy, hooks and provider caches are uncontrolled; fresh sessions do not imply cold caches.",
    "The two Claude full-context answers fail the word protocol, so their numeric differences are not clean protocol-passing matched comparisons.",
    "Codex task B focused score is 9.5 versus full 10 despite both clearing the predeclared threshold.",
    "Codex zero-tools enforcement is requested/audited with read-only and deny-all settings, weaker than hard prevention of every MCP call.",
    "Local supervision does not prove provider-side cancellation; no run timed out.",
    "This session uses these hosted research worker invocations; it does not establish token savings for the enclosing Desktop conversation or whole ecosystem."
  ],
